      "paragraph": "Shipping a computer abroad can require permission when it contains restricted chips. Think of a delivery waiting while the sender checks which permits cover the equipment and its destination. The Financial Times reported on November 26 that Nvidia told manufacturing partners to halt server shipments containing its chips to Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand and Indonesia. Reuters relayed the report and said it could not immediately verify it. Reuters also reported that new US restrictions require export licences for some advanced chips sent to those countries. If the reported pause is confirmed, the affected orders and how long they will wait remain unclear.",
